@echo off
rem Catalyst scan — every 10 min, 09:30-13:00 IST Mon-Fri (Task: TradingBot\CatalystScan).
rem Invokes Claude Code headless to WebSearch catalysts for tickers that just signalled.
rem LOCAL task: writes catalysts.jsonl in the working tree (the scanner reads it directly),
rem so it does NOT git-commit (avoids branch/commit noise on the local tweettweak checkout).
cd /d C:\Users\saikr\Downloads\abundance-trading-bot
"C:\Users\saikr\.local\bin\claude.exe" -p "India catalyst-scan (unattended, local). Do this concisely, no commentary: (1) run: python scripts/pending_catalysts.py --json  (defaults to today IST); parse the ticker list; if empty, stop and do nothing else. (2) For each pending ticker (max 5), use WebSearch to find its latest catalyst in the last 48h (company-specific news, earnings, block deals, guidance) with a source URL; classify polarity as positive, negative, or none (direction-agnostic - it describes the news, not the trade). (3) Compute today's IST date YYYY-MM-DD, then write by piping a JSON array of objects {ticker,polarity,summary,source} to: python scripts/build_catalysts.py --date THAT_DATE --stdin. (4) If at least one catalyst was found, send Telegram via: bash scripts/notify.sh with a compact message, one line per ticker: an emoji (green=positive, red=negative, white=none), the ticker, a <=12-word summary, and [source]. Do NOT run any git command. Do NOT place or propose any trade. Do NOT fabricate a catalyst - but if you genuinely find no material news for a ticker, still record it with polarity 'none' and summary 'no fresh catalyst found' so it counts as researched (do NOT leave it out). Do NOT create .env." --allowedTools "Bash,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep,WebSearch" --dangerously-skip-permissions --model claude-sonnet-5 >> logs\catalyst_scan.log 2>&1
